From 00302c5cc09720d991c4bf2d12612f63139dfa35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Victor Ocsa Mamani <aocsa.cs@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:24:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(starrocks-cn): return the parquet footer row total
 with the FILES() schema

The CN already opens every parquet footer to infer the FILES() schema; it now
sums FileMetaData::num_rows over them and returns the total in a new proto2
field, PGetFileSchemaResult.num_rows = 3 (optional, so a stock FE ignores it
and a stock BE never sets it). Exact-or-absent: a node that samples files must
leave it unset, never send a partial sum. The FE prefers the total over the
bytes / width estimate, which makes the leaf cardinalities exact (lineitem
5,999,989,709 instead of 1,230,652,806) and independent of the dataset copy.

build.rs gains a second guard naming the missing patch, and CI applies every
patches/*.patch through apply-starrocks-patches.sh instead of the nixl patch
by name. The FE patch is regenerated with the one consumption line and its
test. Zero extra I/O on the schema RPC.

Tested: cargo test -p sirius-starrocks-cn --no-default-features (157 lib
tests; new file_schema and get_file_schema tests incl. the routed RPC and its
error path), clippy -D warnings, fmt; FE JUnit testFooterRowCountPreferred
(1000 / null / 0 / -5); fe-build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
